===Scrapped Skin Concepts===
====Candy Apple Blot====
During development of the {{HT|Halloween}} [[Skins]], a Candy Apple Skin for {{CI|Blot|name=true}} was scrapped. This Skin had Blot as a candy apple, with his "hair" resembling caramel, along with having caramel on his feet and on his neck line. He had chartreuse legs and face paint, and his shirt was changed to a more red-orange-ish tone. He also had what appears to be a wooden dowel on his head, akin to the ones real caramel apples have.
<gallery>
Scrapped Candy Apple Skin.png|Scrapped Candy Apple Blot
</gallery>

====Glasses Boxten====
In the 6th of September Art Stream, there was a very early and unfinished [[Skin]] for {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}. The only changes from his original design were a pair of glasses and a shirt. He also appeared to have short pants.
<gallery>
Glasses Boxten.png|Scrapped Glasses Boxten Skin
</gallery>

====Spooky Looey====
During development of the {{HT|Halloween}} [[Skins]], a Spooky Skin for {{CI|Looey|name=true}} was scrapped. This Skin features Looey with a similar color palette to his default, however the green has been switched out for orange and the purple and yellow are in slightly different tones, looking a bit more "sour." He also has green blush and his shirt has a black and green striped pattern. The color scheme also looked similar to Yatta's {{Skin|Infected Candy}} Skin.
<gallery>
Scrapped Spooky Skin.png|Scrapped Spooky Looey Skin
</gallery>

====Ruby and Sapphire Razzle & Dazzle====
In the 2nd of September 2024 Art Stream, an unfinished [[Skin]] for {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} was shown. Razzle's side was colored red and Dazzle's side was colored light blue, their ribbon neck/scarf was colored purple, and they wore a white sweater which was most likely unfinished and the shape of it was reused for the Seafoam Razzle & Dazzle Skin. Noticeably, they don't have any face markings in the concept art, showing that this concept was unfinished.

The idea of the red, blue and purple colors was likely repurposed for the Radiant Dream Razzle & Dazzle Skin, instead using a darker blue color than the unused concept design.
<gallery>
Ruby & Sapphire Razzle & Dazzle.png|Scrapped Ruby and Sapphire Skin
Radiant Dream.png|The {{Skin|Radiant Dream}} Skin in-game
</gallery>

====Dragon Scraps====
In the 2nd of September 2024 Art Stream, the Dragon {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} was shown, a [[Skin]] that was eventually scrapped. She had fully light green skin, her ears were replaced by a pair of horns with yellow tips, her cupcake liner dress has a solid yellow border, and her hands, feet, nails and tail cup are a darker shade. Similar to {{CI|Twisted Scraps|name=true}}, the cup on her tail is now torn, with some noting it resembles a smirk.

An alternate red version of this Skin was possibly going to be used as a [[2025 Halloween Event]] Skin. In this second variant, Scraps was recolored into different shades of red and wears a deep maroon dress. However, due to Scraps' model not being optimized by the time the Event released, the Skin concept has been scrapped entirely.
<gallery>
Scrapped Skin.jpeg|Scrapped Dragon Scraps Skin
Scrapped Scrap skin 2.0.webp|Ditto, but a red version
</gallery>

====Tamagotchi Vee====
In the 2nd of September 2024 Art Stream, two versions of Tamagotchi {{CI|Vee|name=true}} were concepts intended for Vee before being scrapped. In both versions, her limbs were white, her screen displayed a cat mouth, and her microphone had a white grill.

In the first version, Vee's head and body were pale pink, her face display was yellow, her microphone's base was silver, and both her bow-tie and antennas were baby blue. In an alternate design, her bow-tie has yellow polka dots. This Skin's palette was later repurposed for Pastel Paper {{CI|Scraps|name=true}}.

In the second version, her head and body were colored with a blue and yellow marbled pattern, her face display was pale blue, and both her bow-tie and antennas were blue. Her monitor had white stars on its side, and her microphone's base was blue.
